    "unit_type": "paragraph",
    "classification": "clinical_marker",
    "content_hash": "ed163b7bcbc10e9bb4500455a0e57b223f7668c95156e4fbad725de07ba09f99",
    "text": "Eplerenone or spironolactone is recommended for all patients with HFrEF to reduce mortality and the risk of HF hospitalization (Class I, Level A).",
    "table_data": null,
    "section_id": "sec_4_1_2",
    "heading_level": null,
    "breadcrumb": "4. Pharmacological treatments for heart failure with reduced ejection fraction > 4.1. Disease-modifying drug therapy > 4.1.2. Mineralocorticoid receptor antagonists",
